 "fieldData": {
  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Staff Record Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is an employee information form?\", \"a\": \"An employee information form is the record an employer keeps on each person: legal name, contact details, job title, start date, and emergency contacts. HR collects it at hiring and goes back to it whenever payroll or a manager needs a detail.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I make an employee information form online?\", \"a\": \"List the fields payroll and HR use, decide who may see each one, then put a database behind the form. Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder'>AI form builder</a> creates the form, the employee record and the yearly confirmation from one description.\"}, {\"q\": \"What do I need on an employee information form to put someone on payroll?\", \"a\": \"Payroll needs the person's legal name and Social Security number as shown on their card, a home address and a signed Form W-4. Employers also complete Form I-9, and many collect bank details through a direct deposit form.\"}, {\"q\": \"How to fill out an ADP employee information form?\", \"a\": \"Use the version your employer sends and enter your legal name exactly as it reads on your Social Security card. Give a current home address and a phone you answer. If a field is unclear, ask HR before guessing, since payroll copies these answers as written.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is there an employee information form template?\", \"a\": \"Yes. A typical employee information form template fits on one page, grouped by section, with a signature line at the bottom. Paper suits a small team. Past a few dozen people, keeping every copy current becomes the hard part.\"}, {\"q\": \"Where can I get an employee information form PDF?\", \"a\": \"Payroll providers and template sites publish one-page versions. An employee information form PDF suits a single hire, but each answer gets retyped into payroll, and paper never tells HR when someone moves.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is there a free employee information form?\", \"a\": \"Several template sites let you download a free employee information form. Emergent is free to start as well, and its free tier covers building and publishing an online version that saves each answer to a record you can update.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can I make an employee information form in Word?\", \"a\": \"Yes. A two-column table works well: labels on the left, blanks on the right, grouped under bold section headings. Restrict editing to the blanks before you send it, or people type over the labels and the file comes back hard to read.\"}, {\"q\": \"What goes on a basic new employee information form?\", \"a\": \"A basic version asks for legal name, address, phone, personal email, date of birth, job title, start date and one emergency contact. Tax and work eligibility forms travel with it in a new employee form packet.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is there a printable employee information form?\", \"a\": \"Most templates print on one page. Leave room for long addresses, and print single-sided so the sheet scans cleanly into the personnel file. Supervisors who need contacts on site can keep a separate emergency contact form at the front desk.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
 }
}